1
00:00:25,490 --> 00:00:29,240
Humanity was suddenly reminded that day...

2
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:38,210
...of the terror of being at their mercy...

3
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:45,590
...of the humiliation
of being trapped inside a cage...

4
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,030
All soldiers, prepare for battle!

5
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,700
We have one target!

6
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,700
We will slay it and claim this spot

7
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:12,200
as humanity's first stronghold
beyond the walls!

8
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,370
Target approaching!

9
00:01:19,790 --> 00:01:21,630
Split into five groups just as we practiced!

10
00:01:22,710 --> 00:01:24,920
We'll act as the bait!

11
00:01:25,130 --> 00:01:27,760
All assault squads,
switch to omni-directional gear!

12
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:51,610
Strike from all directions at once!

13
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,410
Taste the power...

14
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,170
...of humanity!

15
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:23,060
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

16
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:28,530
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

17
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:33,610
Prayers won't solve anything

18
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:38,950
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

19
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:44,250
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

20
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:46,790
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

21
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,670
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

22
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:55,050
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

23
00:02:55,260 --> 00:03:00,350
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

24
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:05,560
consumed with surging bloodlust,

25
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:12,700
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

26
00:03:34,986 --> 00:03:39,991
To You, in 2000 Years: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 1

27
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:09,790
Huh? Mikasa...

28
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,670
We should be getting back.

29
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:15,880
What are we doing here...?

30
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:19,050
You were that deep asleep
that you're still only half-awake?

31
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,430
No...

32
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:25,480
It just feels like I had this
really long dream or something...

33
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:28,520
What was it about?

34
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:30,650
I can't remember...

35
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:37,030
Eren. Why are you crying?

36
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,410
Huh?

37
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:49,250
Listen!

38
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:52,590
It was by God's great wisdom
that the walls were built!

39
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:56,090
The walls are His divine work!

40
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:00,050
No one must be allowed to defile the walls!

41
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:07,180
Don't you dare tell anyone I was crying.

42
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,100
I won't.

43
00:05:09,310 --> 00:05:12,770
Still, crying for no real reason...

44
00:05:12,980 --> 00:05:15,070
You should have your dad give you a checkup.

45
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:18,780
Don't be stupid! I can't tell him!

46
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:20,820
What are you cryin' about, Eren?

47
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:24,580
Mr. Hannes...

48
00:05:24,790 --> 00:05:27,040
Did Mikasa get on your case about somethin'?

49
00:05:27,250 --> 00:05:29,750
Huh?! What makes you think I was crying?!

50
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,750
Whoa, you reek of alcohol!

51
00:05:32,710 --> 00:05:34,090
It's like, come on, y'know?

52
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:35,550
Oh.

53
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:37,300
You're drinking again...

54
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:39,130
You guys wanna join in?

55
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,760
Actually, uhh... Don't you have work?

56
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:44,470
Yup! We're guardin' the gate today!

57
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:49,810
We're stuck here all day,
so we end up getting hungry and thirsty.

58
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:55,730
If some booze happens to get into our drinks,
so what? It's no big deal.

59
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,610
What if something happens?!
Can you fight like that?!

60
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:03,700
- Whadya mean, "If something happens"?
- You know what I mean!

61
00:06:03,910 --> 00:06:06,950
I'm talking about if
they break the walls and get into the city!

62
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:11,920
Oww...

63
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:15,380
Geez, Eren. Don't go yellin' like that.

64
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:19,550
You've got spunk, doctor's son!

65
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:23,840
If they do bust down the walls,
we'll take care of business, don't you worry.

66
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:28,140
But that ain't happened once
in the last one hundred years.

67
00:06:28,350 --> 00:06:33,690
Still, my dad says there's nothing
more dangerous than being complacent like that!

68
00:06:33,900 --> 00:06:35,810
Dr. Jaeger, huh?

69
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,480
Yeah, he's got a point.

70
00:06:37,690 --> 00:06:42,200
He once saved this town from an epidemic.

71
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:44,740
I can't argue with him.

72
00:06:44,950 --> 00:06:47,830
Still, they're another story altogether.

73
00:06:49,330 --> 00:06:53,040
When you're a soldier, you get to see
those things roaming around outside

74
00:06:53,250 --> 00:06:55,790
while you're on
wall reinforcement duty and stuff.

75
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:00,840
These walls are fifty meters tall, though.
I can't see 'em getting through.

76
00:07:01,050 --> 00:07:05,840
Then... you're not actually
prepared to fight them at all?!

77
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:06,930
Nope!

78
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:09,310
Wh-What?!

79
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:12,060
Then drop the "Garrison Regiment" name

80
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,060
for "Wall Construction Squad" instead!

81
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,940
Not a bad idea!

82
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,690
But you gotta understand, Eren.

83
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:23,070
If a soldier's doing his job,
things have seriously gone to hell.

84
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,740
It's better when everyone's
calling us useless freeloaders;

85
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:30,200
it means peaceful times for us all.

86
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:36,830
Sure, we can stay
inside the walls our entire lives

87
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,800
and do nothing but eat and sleep!

88
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,840
But... that basically...

89
00:07:44,050 --> 00:07:46,220
That basically makes us cattle!

90
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,560
Man, you're one plucky kid, all right!

91
00:07:51,770 --> 00:07:55,190
For someone who's totally helpless!
Right, Hannes?!

92
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:57,100
Huh? Y-Yeah.

93
00:07:58,730 --> 00:08:00,570
Hey! Eren!

94
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:04,280
What a weirdo!

95
00:08:04,490 --> 00:08:08,740
Wait... Don't tell me
he wants to join the Scout Regiment?

96
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:21,750
Eren. I'd forget about
the Scout Regiment if I were you.

97
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:25,340
What?! You think the Scout Regiment
is a joke too?!

98
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:28,050
It's not about what I think.

99
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:37,230
The Scout Regiment is back!

100
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,980
They're gonna open the front gate!

101
00:08:39,190 --> 00:08:41,900
Let's go see the heroes return, Mikasa!

102
00:08:42,110 --> 00:08:43,070
Ohm!

103
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,710
Damn! I can't see!

104
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:28,360
They're the only ones who made it back?

105
00:09:28,570 --> 00:09:31,030
Everyone else must've gotten eaten.

106
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:34,370
This is what they get
for going outside the walls.

107
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:36,910
Moses! Moses!

108
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,660
Excuse me...

109
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:41,380
I don't see my son Moses anywhere...

110
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:43,590
Do you know where he is?

111
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:47,130
This is Moses' mother.

112
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:48,670
Go get it.

113
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:17,490
It's all we could retrieve.

114
00:10:33,930 --> 00:10:35,890
But... my son...

115
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,390
He was helpful, yes?

116
00:10:39,930 --> 00:10:43,150
Even if he didn't achieve direct greatness...

117
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:48,730
...surely my son's death
helped humanity fight back, yes?!

118
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,490
Of course...!

119
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:02,210
No...

120
00:11:02,410 --> 00:11:05,750
On this latest scouting mission, we...

121
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:07,090
No...

122
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:10,920
Just like all the other missions...

123
00:11:11,130 --> 00:11:15,470
...we achieved nothing at all!

124
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:18,010
My incompetence has done nothing

125
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:20,890
but needlessly send soldiers to their deaths!

126
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:27,730
We haven't found out anything about them!

127
00:11:33,650 --> 00:11:35,030
Talk about gruesome.

128
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,030
You can say that again.

129
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:41,500
Our taxes are basically going
to feeding and fattening those things up now.

130
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:46,710
What the hell, you little punk?!

131
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:51,670
H-Hey! What are you doing, Mikasa?!

132
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:54,090
Hey! Get back here, you!

133
00:11:55,930 --> 00:11:58,760
Mikasa! Enough already!

134
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:07,190
What's the big idea?!
Now the firewood's all over the place!

135
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,860
Eren.

136
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:13,530
Have you changed your mind
about joining the Scout Regiment?

137
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:24,160
Help pick this up.

138
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:27,290
It's not that bad of a mess.

139
00:12:44,310 --> 00:12:45,810
We're home.

140
00:12:47,230 --> 00:12:48,730
Welcome back.

141
00:12:51,730 --> 00:12:55,650
Wow, Eren! You actually worked hard!

142
00:12:55,860 --> 00:12:57,150
Yeah...

143
00:13:00,490 --> 00:13:01,740
What do you want?

144
00:13:01,950 --> 00:13:05,200
Your ear's red. That shows that you're lying.

145
00:13:05,410 --> 00:13:07,830
You had Mikasa help you, didn't you?

146
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:11,670
Oh? You're leaving, Dad?

147
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:12,710
Is it for work?

148
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:15,420
Yes. Some checkups in the interior.

149
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:17,340
It'll take a couple of days.

150
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:24,220
Eren says he wants to join the Scout Regiment.

151
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:30,020
M-Mikasa! I told you not to say anything!

152
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:31,520
Eren!

153
00:13:31,730 --> 00:13:33,400
What are you thinking?!

154
00:13:33,610 --> 00:13:37,530
Do you have any idea how many people
have died outside the walls?!

155
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,860
- Y-Yeah, I know!
- Then...!

156
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:41,570
Eren.

157
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:45,660
Why do you want to go out there?

158
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:50,920
I want to know what the outside world is like!

159
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:55,300
I don't want to live my entire life
in ignorance inside the walls!

160
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:57,210
Plus...

161
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:00,470
If no one else is willing to take their place,

162
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:03,800
then the lives of all who've died
will be for nothing!

163
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:09,020
I see.

164
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:13,310
My boat's about to leave. I better get going.

165
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,480
Hold on, dear! Talk some sense into Eren!

166
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:17,780
Carla.

167
00:14:17,980 --> 00:14:23,370
Words can't hold back human curiosity.

168
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:24,660
Eren.

169
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:28,700
When I get back, I'll show you the basement

170
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:31,410
that I've kept secret all this time.

171
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:33,120
R-Really?!

172
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,840
Take care!

173
00:14:41,090 --> 00:14:43,470
Just forget it.

174
00:14:43,680 --> 00:14:45,220
Joining the Scout Regiment is a stupid idea!

175
00:14:45,430 --> 00:14:47,390
Huh?! Stupid?!

176
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:52,600
People who don't mind living like livestock
are the stupid ones, if you ask me!

177
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:54,020
Eren!

178
00:14:57,110 --> 00:14:58,280
Mikasa.

179
00:14:58,480 --> 00:15:01,110
He gets himself into trouble so easily.

180
00:15:01,320 --> 00:15:04,030
If anything ever happens,
you need to be there for each other!

181
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,530
Mm.

182
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:11,000
What's the matter, heretic?!

183
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,870
If you don't like it, let's see you hit back!

184
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:16,500
Y-Yeah, right!

185
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:18,840
That would be stooping to your level!

186
00:15:19,050 --> 00:15:20,090
Say what?!

187
00:15:20,300 --> 00:15:23,470
You know I'm right!

188
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,970
That's why you have to resort to violence!
Because you can't argue back!

189
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:30,390
Which means you
concede defeat to me, does it not?!

190
00:15:31,810 --> 00:15:34,060
Shut up, smart-ass!

191
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:35,350
Stop that!

192
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,650
It's Eren!

193
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:41,740
- That Idiot's back for more?!
- Does he want his ass kicked?!

194
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,570
We'll tear you a new one!

195
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:47,070
M-Mikasa's with him!

196
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,870
S-Screw this! Let's get outta here!

197
00:15:55,370 --> 00:15:58,000
One look at me and they ran off!

198
00:15:58,210 --> 00:16:00,750
No, it was Mikasa they saw...

199
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,170
Oww!

200
00:16:02,380 --> 00:16:04,380
Hey! You Okay. Armin?!

201
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,810
I can get up on my own...

202
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,390
Oh.

203
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:20,190
I said humanity needs to venture
into the outside world at some point...

204
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:22,530
...and then they beat me up
and called me a heretic.

205
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:24,030
Damn...

206
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:29,490
Why does everyone look down on people
just for wanting to go outside?!

207
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:32,540
Well, because we've had
a hundred years of peace

208
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:34,950
by staying inside the walls.

209
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:37,210
They're worried that going outside carelessly

210
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:40,210
will invite them inside the walls.

211
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:42,420
The royal government's policies have made

212
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:46,420
having any interest
in the outside world a taboo.

213
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:49,760
It's our lives! We can risk 'em if we want!

214
00:16:49,970 --> 00:16:51,510
Absolutely not.

215
00:16:53,390 --> 00:16:54,600
Forget about it.

216
00:16:54,810 --> 00:16:57,560
Which reminds me,
I can't believe you told my parents!

217
00:16:57,770 --> 00:16:58,560
Huh?

218
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:00,270
I never agreed to help.

219
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,270
So, what did they say?

220
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:05,740
They're... less than pleased.

221
00:17:07,150 --> 00:17:08,490
It figures.

222
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:15,160
Indeed, I think people are crazy

223
00:17:15,370 --> 00:17:19,460
if they think we'll be
safe inside these walls forever.

224
00:17:19,670 --> 00:17:20,830
Mommy!

225
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:26,800
Just because the walls
haven't fallen for a hundred years

226
00:17:27,010 --> 00:17:29,720
doesn't guarantee that they won't fall today...

227
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,050
And yet...

228
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:53,450
Wh-What was that?!

229
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:54,870
An explosion?!

230
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:57,250
- That way!
- Did something fall?!

231
00:17:57,450 --> 00:17:59,710
I'm not really sure...

232
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:02,420
Hey, Armin!

233
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,840
What is it?! What do you see?!

234
00:18:19,430 --> 00:18:20,850
It can't be...!

235
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:25,610
Th-That wall... is fifty meters high!

236
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,530
It's one of them...

237
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:35,330
A Titan!

238
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:25,790
L-it... opened a hole in the wall...

239
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,010
They're inside!

240
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:34,680
The Titans have gotten inside!

241
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,010
We need to run too!

242
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,100
Eren!

243
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:43,180
My house is in that direction!

244
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,440
Mom...!

245
00:19:45,650 --> 00:19:46,690
Mikasa!

246
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:55,110
It's all over...

247
00:19:55,320 --> 00:20:01,620
Countless Titans... are going to overrun the city!

248
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:09,210
It couldn't have hit our home!

249
00:20:09,420 --> 00:20:12,710
Just around this corner...
our house is standing there, like always!

250
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:18,600
Mom!

251
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:22,350
Mom!

252
00:20:24,180 --> 00:20:26,560
- Eren!
- Mikasa! Grab that end!

253
00:20:26,770 --> 00:20:28,270
We gotta move this pillar!

254
00:20:47,170 --> 00:20:48,170
Hurry, Mikasa!

255
00:20:48,370 --> 00:20:50,130
I know!

256
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:53,380
The Titans have gotten inside, haven't they?

257
00:20:53,590 --> 00:20:55,760
Eren! Take Mikasa and run away!

258
00:20:55,970 --> 00:20:57,130
Hurry!

259
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,970
I want to!

260
00:20:59,180 --> 00:21:01,510
So hurry and get out of there!

261
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:05,140
The debris has crushed my legs...

262
00:21:05,350 --> 00:21:08,980
Even if I could get out,
I wouldn't be able to run.

263
00:21:09,190 --> 00:21:09,980
You understand what that means.

264
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:11,940
I'll carry you, then!

265
00:21:12,150 --> 00:21:15,280
Why don't you ever listen to your mother?!

266
00:21:15,490 --> 00:21:18,200
You can at least do this one last thing!

267
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,570
Mikasa!

268
00:21:20,530 --> 00:21:22,080
No...

269
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:23,910
No...!

270
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,200
If you don't go, all three of us will...

271
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,210
Hannes!

272
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,460
Take the children and get out of here!

273
00:21:34,670 --> 00:21:37,420
Don't go underestimatin' me, Carla.

274
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:41,890
I'm gonna slaughter these Titans
and save all three of ya!

275
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:44,600
Wait! Don't fight them!

276
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,850
Yeah, I could save those two for sure.

277
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:49,310
But now...

278
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:52,020
I'm finally going to repay the favor I owe!

279
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:10,330
Hey! Mr. Hannes!

280
00:22:10,540 --> 00:22:12,460
What are you doing?!

281
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:15,170
- Thank you...
- Hey!

282
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:18,090
Mom's still...!

283
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:21,050
Eren! Mikasa!

284
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:23,640
You have to survive!

285
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:38,190
Don't go...

286
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:52,120
Stop!

287
00:23:25,410 --> 00:23:29,290
Humanity was suddenly reminded that day...

288
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:37,000
...of the terror of being at their mercy...

289
00:23:39,170 --> 00:23:44,340
...of the humiliation
of being trapped inside a cage...

290
00:24:09,530 --> 00:24:14,250
Your dreams are where your heart is

291
00:24:14,460 --> 00:24:20,500
They're more fragile than life itself

292
00:24:20,710 --> 00:24:25,220
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

293
00:24:25,420 --> 00:24:31,930
Now, rest in peace

294
00:24:32,140 --> 00:24:43,030
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

295
00:24:43,230 --> 00:24:53,540
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

296
00:24:53,740 --> 00:24:59,500
In this beautiful, cruel world

297
00:24:59,710 --> 00:25:04,800
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

298
00:25:05,010 --> 00:25:10,430
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

299
00:25:10,640 --> 00:25:15,980
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

300
00:25:16,180 --> 00:25:20,770
to anything anymore?

301
00:25:26,860 --> 00:25:28,950
Shiganshina falls.

302
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:34,490
Prayers, screams, and death
are all that humanity is allowed.

303
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,466
Amid this, Eren alone
swears revenge in his small heart.

304
00:25:37,466 --> 00:25:39,790
That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2
Amid this, Eren alone
swears revenge in his small heart.

305
00:25:39,790 --> 00:25:39,930
That Day: The Fall of Shiganshina, Part 2
